{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jack and Jill exercise along the same route. Jill jogs the first half of the route at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fc355ce082a89913650cb3af6b936b0f5e8813f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, runs the remainder of the route at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a9310508df314c2851e8a4ebbefc61e308bf87e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and takes a total time of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> hours. Jack walks the first third of the route at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c5efb842d1faa25cff38d42d59213b78638151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, runs the remainder at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6098a7ead95ac18edfc78879bd6117c20a9da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and takes a total time of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> hours. Which of the following is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d783347dc9059f615d5444a5ec6e23df3229ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/2774cb26e22074fc602a94a8165350955f15238c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{9}{8}  \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{7}{5}  \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{15}{16}  \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{9}{16}  \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{10}{9}  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"431\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the total distance of the route. Jill goes travels the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47d94c940dbfd5dcd6930004c9b078c734fd9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}D\\text{ km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fc355ce082a89913650cb3af6b936b0f5e8813f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47d94c940dbfd5dcd6930004c9b078c734fd9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}D\\text{ km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a9310508df314c2851e8a4ebbefc61e308bf87e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and the total time spent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> hours. Using dimensional analysis, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\tx\\text{ hours} &amp;= \\dfrac{1\\text{ hour}}{6\\text{ km}} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}D\\ \\text{km} + \\dfrac{1\\text{ hour}}{12\\text{ km}} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}D \\text{ km}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\dfrac{D}{12}\\text{ hours} + \\dfrac{D}{24}\\text{ hours}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\dfrac{2D}{24}\\text{ hours} + \\dfrac{D}{24}\\text{ hours}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\dfrac{D}{8}\\text{ hours}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Similarly, Jack travels the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb64f6d8a79f2e702ee9a86c55128fa6d934d12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{3}D\\text{ km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c5efb842d1faa25cff38d42d59213b78638151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and she the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550e636cbecfb165337c84c8cd281afede9e894f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2}{3}D\\text{ km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6098a7ead95ac18edfc78879bd6117c20a9da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\text{ km/h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and the total time spent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> hours. Using dimensional analysis, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\ty\\text{ hours} &amp;= \\dfrac{1\\text{ hour}}{5\\text{ km}} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{3}D \\text{ km} + \\dfrac{1\\text{ hour}}{15\\text{ km}} \\cdot \\dfrac{2}{3}D \\text{ km}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\dfrac{D}{15}\\text{ hours} + \\dfrac{2D}{45}\\text{ hours}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\dfrac{3D}{45}\\text{ hours} + \\dfrac{2D}{45}\\text{ hours}\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\dfrac{D}{9}\\text{ hours}\n\\end{align*}\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc4016681a09e06ed646fe24ebaf9bb8b94920e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x}{y} = \\dfrac{D/8}{D/9} = \\dfrac{D}{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{9}{D} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{9}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"238\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" titl